The potential vulnerability is related to an Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR). This vulnerability arises because the API design allows direct access to image resources through their identifiers (`imageId`) without implementing proper access control mechanisms. If the `imageId` is predictable or not sufficiently protected, an attacker could manipulate the `imageId` parameter to access or view images they are not authorized to see. This lack of robust authorization checks can lead to unauthorized access to sensitive or private data, compromising the confidentiality and security of the application.

